**/coverage

# TypeScript's incremental build state. This one is not obvious and it breaks
# the image in a way that looks like a source error.
#
# `dist` is excluded above so the container builds its own. But a copied
# .tsbuildinfo tells tsc the output is already up to date, so tsc emits
# nothing — leaving every package with no dist and every consumer failing on
# "has no exported member". The symptom points at the source; the cause is
# stale build state that was never meant to be in the image.
**/*.tsbuildinfo
.git
.github
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
docs
*.md
*.pdf
*.docx
playwright-report
test-results
docker-compose.yml
